   "source": [
    "# Detecção de Anomalias em Transações\n",
    "\n",
    "Projeto de detecção de transações fraudulentas com Python e Machine Learning.\n",
    "\n",
    "A estrutura acompanha as etapas apresentadas na atividade da DIO. Na etapa de SMOTE, o balanceamento é aplicado somente ao conjunto de treinamento para evitar data leakage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "344a61f1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Instalação das bibliotecas"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "68ea9e01",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip -q install imbalanced-learn xgboost shap"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bf17ac51",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Importação das bibliotecas"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "668898d2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, GridSearchCV\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
    "    classification_report, confusion_matrix,\n",
    "    roc_curve, roc_auc_score, precision_recall_curve\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "from imblearn.over_sampling import SMOTE\n",
    "from xgboost import XGBClassifier\n",
    "import shap\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.set_option(\"display.max_columns\", None)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "64f639a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Carregamento dos dados"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "75323955",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = pd.read_csv(\"creditcard.csv\")\n",
    "print(\"Dimensões do dataset:\", df.shape)\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a1bc0d88",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Análise exploratória"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4696fde0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Informações do dataset:\")\n",
    "df.info()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nTotal de valores nulos:\")\n",
    "print(df.isnull().sum().sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nDistribuição da variável Class:\")\n",
    "print(df[\"Class\"].value_counts())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nDistribuição proporcional:\")\n",
    "print(df[\"Class\"].value_counts(normalize=True))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c18c2d8c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretação\n",
    "\n",
    "`Class = 0` representa uma transação normal e `Class = 1` representa fraude.\n",
    "\n",
    "O dataset é fortemente desbalanceado. Portanto, accuracy isoladamente não é suficiente para avaliar o problema."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8b88af29",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[\"Class\"].value_counts(normalize=True).plot(\n",
    "    kind=\"bar\", title=\"Proporção das classes\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Class\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Proporção\")\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=0)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1f9f3ff5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Transformação logarítmica do Amount"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a5fb6bf3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[\"Amount_log\"] = np.log1p(df[\"Amount\"])\n",
    "df[[\"Amount\", \"Amount_log\"]].head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e593632b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Padronização do Amount"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "42e7f6f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "df[\"Amount_scaled\"] = scaler.fit_transform(df[[\"Amount\"]])\n",
    "df[[\"Amount\", \"Amount_log\", \"Amount_scaled\"]].head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b12471f9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Separação entre X e y"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9a849b4f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X = df.drop(\"Class\", axis=1)\n",
    "y = df[\"Class\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"X:\", X.shape)\n",
    "print(\"y:\", y.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4689e991",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Train/Test Split"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8867c0ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X, y, stratify=y, test_size=0.3, random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Treino:\", X_train.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Teste:\", X_test.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Fraudes no treino:\", y_train.sum())\n",
    "print(\"Fraudes no teste:\", y_test.sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5378bd43",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Regressão Logística"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f479eec4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)\n",
    "model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "y_pred = model.predict(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8c9b1234",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Curva ROC"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "151d595e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "y_probs = model.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "fpr, tpr, _ = roc_curve(y_test, y_probs)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.plot(fpr, tpr)\n",
    "plt.title(\"ROC Curve\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"False Positive Rate\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"True Positive Rate\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"AUC:\", round(roc_auc_score(y_test, y_probs), 4))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4623740e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Curva Precision-Recall"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d6226484",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "precision, recall, _ = precision_recall_curve(y_test, y_probs)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.plot(recall, precision)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Precision-Recall Curve\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Recall\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Precision\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e2b676d3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Random Forest"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4608970b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rf = RandomForestClassifier(\n",
    "    n_estimators=50,\n",
    "    max_depth=10,\n",
    "    class_weight=\"balanced\",\n",
    "    n_jobs=-1,\n",
    "    random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "rf.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "y_pred_rf = rf.predict(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred_rf))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ef7c6ef7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 13. Balanceamento — Undersampling"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fd552f0a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fraudes = df[df[\"Class\"] == 1]\n",
    "normais = df[df[\"Class\"] == 0].sample(len(fraudes), random_state=42)\n",
    "df_under = pd.concat([fraudes, normais])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(df_under[\"Class\"].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1d2e7076",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 14. Balanceamento — SMOTE\n",
    "\n",
    "O SMOTE é aplicado somente ao conjunto de treinamento, depois da divisão treino/teste, para evitar data leakage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "617a82cc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "smote = SMOTE(random_state=42)\n",
    "X_train_res, y_train_res = smote.fit_resample(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Antes do SMOTE:\")\n",
    "print(y_train.value_counts())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nDepois do SMOTE:\")\n",
    "print(y_train_res.value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "be6722cc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 15. Regressão Logística com SMOTE"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0fa327e4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model_smote = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)\n",
    "model_smote.fit(X_train_res, y_train_res)\n",
    "y_pred_smote = model_smote.predict(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred_smote))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b56927e6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 16. Pipeline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "46dc29a0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"scaler\", StandardScaler()),\n",
    "    (\"model\", LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000))\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "pipeline.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "y_pred_pipeline = pipeline.predict(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred_pipeline))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9bc3d90f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 17. Ajuste de threshold"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fe75a975",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "threshold = 0.3\n",
    "y_pred_custom = (y_probs > threshold).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred_custom))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "94a1a38a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 18. XGBoost"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a7025a0c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "xgb = XGBClassifier(\n",
    "    scale_pos_weight=10,\n",
    "    eval_metric=\"logloss\",\n",
    "    random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "xgb.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "y_pred_xgb = xgb.predict(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred_xgb))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "19328e3e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 19. Importância das variáveis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2472d59e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "importancias = xgb.feature_importances_\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.bar(range(len(importancias)), importancias)\n",
    "plt.title(\"Importância das variáveis\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Índice da variável\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Importância\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cb7fe7be",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 20. GridSearchCV"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "513a7213",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "param_grid = {\n",
    "    \"max_depth\": [3, 5],\n",
    "    \"n_estimators\": [50, 100]\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "grid = GridSearchCV(\n",
    "    XGBClassifier(eval_metric=\"logloss\", random_state=42),\n",
    "    param_grid,\n",
    "    scoring=\"recall\",\n",
    "    cv=3,\n",
    "    n_jobs=-1\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "grid.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Melhor modelo:\", grid.best_params_)\n",
    "print(\"Melhor recall médio:\", round(grid.best_score_, 4))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9e5660ac",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 21. Avaliação do melhor XGBoost"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "76629571",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "best_xgb = grid.best_estimator_\n",
    "y_pred_best_xgb = best_xgb.predict(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred_best_xgb))\n",
    "print(\"Matriz de confusão:\")\n",
    "print(confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred_best_xgb))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f71f3def",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 22. Explicabilidade com SHAP"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3534e496",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "explainer = shap.Explainer(xgb)\n",
    "shap_values = explainer(X_test.iloc[:100])\n",
    "shap.plots.bar(shap_values)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5f64be7e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 23. Conclusão\n",
    "\n",
    "O dataset apresenta forte desbalanceamento entre transações normais e fraudulentas. Por isso, recall, precision, F1-score, ROC-AUC e Precision-Recall são mais informativos do que accuracy isoladamente.\n",
    "\n",
    "Foram comparadas Regressão Logística, Random Forest e XGBoost, além de técnicas de balanceamento, ajuste de threshold, otimização de hiperparâmetros e explicabilidade com SHAP.\n",
    "\n",
    "Em um cenário real, a escolha do modelo e do threshold deve considerar o custo de falsos positivos e falsos negativos."
   ]
  }
